# The branches a release may be cut from, one extended regular expression
# a line that a branch's whole name matches (tools/release-place.sh reads
# it; never a shell glob, whose * also matches a slash and whatever
# follows): a tag's commit has to be on one
# of them, as its remote holds it, or nothing is signed for it. A stable
# release and a release candidate are cut from main alone, whatever is
# listed here; a dev build (vX.Y.Z-dev.N) from any of these.
#
# The job that holds the release key reads the default branch's copy of
# this file and of the script, not the tag's own (build-image.yml,
# seal-release.yml), so a tag cannot name its own branch here.
main
# A release's working branch, named for the version it becomes.
claude/[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+
